# Image dimensions reserve the box

Plain pixel integers survive ingest so the reader can hold the image's aspect ratio while it loads.

![a chart](https://cdn.example.com/chart.png)

Kept as written.

The common `px` slip and stray whitespace are normalized:

![normalized](https://cdn.example.com/photo.jpg)

Percentages, zero, exponents, signs and oversized values are not intrinsic sizes and are dropped:

![percent and zero](https://cdn.example.com/a.png) ![exponent and sign](https://cdn.example.com/b.png) ![oversized and auto](https://cdn.example.com/c.png)

Dimensions mean nothing on other elements: plain text.
